docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1138:## Backup Command Follow-Up
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1140:Implemented an AI-first backup surface under `yalla database backup`:
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1143:yalla database backup create postgres --id postgres_123 --destination-id dst_123 --database app --prefix backups/app/ --schedule "0 2 * * *" --keep-latest 7
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1144:yalla database backup run postgres --backup-id backup_123
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1145:yalla database backup update postgres --backup-id backup_123 --schedule "0 4 * * *" --keep-latest 14
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1146:yalla database backup get --backup-id backup_123
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1147:yalla database backup list-files --destination-id dst_123 --prefix backups/app/
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1148:yalla database backup delete --backup-id backup_123
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1151:Supported engines for backup create/run/update are `postgres`, `mysql`, `mariadb`, and `mongo`. Redis intentionally returns `E_UNSUPPORTED` because the embedded Dokploy backup schema has no Redis backup operation.
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-12-friendly-database-commands.md:1153:`database backup update` is patch-like for agents: it calls `backup-one`, preserves required fields, overlays changed flags, and sends the complete `backup-update` body. `database backup create` emits `backup_id` even when Dokploy's `backup-create` response body is `{}` by recovering the new schedule from the database record's `backups` array (`postgres-one`, `mysql-one`, `mariadb-one`, or `mongo-one`) and falling back to `user-getBackups`.
