@@ -1,4 +1,11 @@
 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Backup operations artifacts follow the static-release-gate pattern:
+  keep `deploy/operations/backup-database.sh`,
+  `deploy/operations/README.md`, SECURITY.md, CI,
+  `scripts/verify.sh`, and `internal/release/*_static_test.go` in lockstep;
+  keep the backup data plane outside Yalla Go processes, run `pg_dump` from
+  the operator shell artifact, update `YALLA_BACKUP_STATUS_FILE` atomically
+  only after success, and redact all `YALLA_*` dry-run values.
 - Production operations commands that mutate control-plane source-of-truth
   state should be pinned by release static tests and route writes through a
   narrow `yalla-api` maintenance flag rather than shell SQL; keep the script,
